### 5. Edge → Conviction drift and flip rates

Favorite gains price between windows in **all 20 cities**. The useful column is
bracket-identity FLIP rate:

- **Las Vegas 8.8% flips**, highest Edge price (66.3¢) — settled early.
- **Los Angeles 35.3% flips, +11.9¢ drift** — identity changes a third of the
  time then resolves harder than anywhere (72.2¢ at Conviction). Strongest
  Conviction city, worst Edge city.
- **Denver 23.7%, Houston 23.1%, Boston 23.0%, Dallas 22.7%** — churning late.
- **Atlanta (14.8%) and Washington DC (18.0%)** — low flip, CHEAPEST Edge prices
  (50.8¢, 49.6¢), near-zero drift. Market prices them as uncertain and they
  aren't actually moving.

Flip rate measures whether the MARKET changed its mind, not whether it was right.

