### Manual grid recommendation for lows (untested — a reasoned guess)

There is no single ET time pair that works nationally: peak heat is
mid-afternoon everywhere, but minima land near local dawn, spread across three
hours of ET clock time. ET cities bottom before 7am ET; western cities near
9:30am ET.

**Grid only Phoenix, Las Vegas, Los Angeles (and optionally Denver) at
8:00am and 9:15am ET** — ~90 min and ~20 min before their median minimum. Same
before/after structure as the highs grid, at sustainable hours. Eastern cities
would need 4:30am/6:30am ET and their markets only open ~1–3am anyway.

These four are also the cheapest, least-converged boards. **Do not treat 8:00/
9:15 as settled** — `lows_snapshots` will give the measured answer in a few
weeks. Phoenix's 23h timing spread means a fixed capture time will sometimes
miss entirely.

